the quiet of a dead forest  a reason perhaps to give up hope  europe's wildfires are the continent's  worst in a hundred years  but nature is resilient and where the  earth is scorched life is returning  though it will almost certainly never be  the same  a few days ago sobreros and spain's  avila province was surrounded by fires  celia morales played in these mountains  as a child  she says it was a magical place for kids  the fires came so close to the town  she filmed the flames from her front  garden  it made me feel very impotent because we  couldn't do anything it was very windy a  lot of people were shouting because they  were very nervous the mountain was full  of grass and brushes and everything  burned really quickly the whole thing  was a nightmare now we need to think  about rehabilitation  for small communities such as sobreros  life  is changing rapidly  climate change means less rain more heat  drier conditions and year on year more  intense wildfires environmental experts  agree that the best case scenario is  this is the new normal  [Music]  on the outskirts of madrid to prevent  future fires one mayor is championing  the old ways  javier de la nieto calls them  his little fireman  fundamentals  goats are essential to prevent fires in  a mediterranean climate like spain  because they are the only ones able to  feed on the leaves fruits and flowers of  plants like this one they clear the area  so fires are not as fast and hot and do  not burn as many hectares  other areas are adopting his program it  is subsidized by firefighters and is  even receiving eu support  where the goats graze he says there has  not been a serious fire in six years  but the spanish government won't let  delaniento use public land fearing over  grazing and a disruption to the natural  environment  however it is too late for that the  disruption he says has already happened  looking at the surrounding hillsides de  la nieto sees a bomb waiting to go off  and perhaps he says  the solution to man-made environmental  disasters  lies in nature itself  zayn vesravia al-jazeera spain
 

